From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Turcios <turcioskevinr@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 23:51:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Identify as kpip

kpip shares pip's configuration, caches and PIP_* environment variables,
but says who it is: --version names kpip and the pip release it is built
from, the program name falls back to kpip, the user agent's installer is
kpip, and installed distributions record INSTALLER as kpip.

Deprecation deadlines and the "pip_version" field of install reports and
inspect output stay in pip versions, which is what they are scheduled and
specified in. The self version check is off: pip's latest release on the
index says nothing about whether kpip is current.
